s=s.replace('The exact equations and update rules appear in the companion methods record.', 'The exact equations and update rules appear in the companion methods record, \\texttt{evidence/method-details.md}.')
s=s.replace(' The technical implementation, including the feature-distribution loss and its weighting, is recorded in the companion methods audit.','')
s=s.replace('Its Random Forest has 100 trees, maximum depth five, square-root feature subsampling, class-balanced training, and seed 42.', 'A Random Forest (RF) combines the predictions of decision trees fitted to these measurements. Here it uses 100 trees, maximum depth five, square-root feature subsampling, class-balanced training, and seed 42.')
s=s.replace('We assess sensitivity to the sampled sources by repeatedly drawing whole source videos, a procedure called a source bootstrap.', 'We assess sensitivity to source composition by repeatedly resampling groups of saved predictions, keeping all clips from a sampled source together. This procedure is called a source bootstrap.')
